# Tech Survivor does not read environment variables from the repo root at runtime.
# Each app has its own env file - copy these before running anything:
#
#   frontend/.env.local.example  ->  frontend/.env.local   (Next.js frontend)
#   backend/.env.example         ->  backend/.env          (Express backend)
#
# The seed/create-admin scripts under scripts/ read backend/.env directly
# (see scripts/package.json), so you only ever need to fill in that one file
# for backend + scripts, plus frontend/.env.local for the frontend.
#
# See README.md "Environment variables" for what each value means and where to get it.
